---
// src/pages/_site-updates/2026-10-31-follow-up-automation-claims.astro
export const updateMeta = {
  date: '2026-10-31',
  title: 'Follow-up automation claims brought in line with the product',
  tags: ['accuracy', 'buyers', 'reminders'],
};
---
<article class="border-l-4 border-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] pl-6">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">October 31, 2026</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-4">
    Reworded the after-placement follow-up claims to describe the reminders BreederHQ
    actually creates for the breeder.
  </p>

  <div class="mb-4">
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">Corrected</h3>
    <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
      <li>The plan comparison no longer lists "Follow-Up Automation." It now reads "Automatic Buyer Check-In Reminders."</li>
      <li>The client management workflow no longer promises six-month and one-year milestone follow-ups or health testing reminders for co-owned animals. It describes a 30-day check-in reminder after placement, a yearly birthday reminder, and vaccination expiration alerts, all delivered to the breeder, who does the outreach.</li>
      <li>The Breeder CRM page's after-sale step no longer lists six-month check-ins and says what is automatic and what the breeder sends.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</article>
